    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green. Here's a summary of the change \u2014 owner deletion is now a soft-delete.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**1. `Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`)\nAdded a `deleted` boolean column (default `false`) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()`. A newly created owner is `false`.\n\n**2. Delete pipeline** (`rest/function/owner/DeleteOwner.java`)\nReplaced the hard `ownerRepository.delete(owner)` with a soft-delete: set `deleted = true` and `save`, retaining the row. The `DELETE.yml` pipeline (load \u2192 delete \u2192 respond 204) is unchanged \u2014 it still returns 2xx, and `GET /api/owners/{id}` still loads the row (now with `deleted: true`).\n\n**3. Create-time duplicate/identity checks**\n- `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` (the blocking 409 guard) now skips soft-deleted owners, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only match is deleted.\n- `AssignPossibleDuplicate` (the soft-duplicate flag) also skips deleted owners, per the spec's \"duplicate and identity checks must ignore deleted owners.\"\n\n**4. API contract** (`openapi.yml`)\nAdded a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema. The generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct maps it automatically, so GET responses expose `deleted`.\n\n**5. Schemas** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres`)\nAdded a `deleted` column (NOT NULL, default false) to the `owners` table. Tests run on hsqldb; the others were updated for consistency.\n\n## Test results\n```\nAcceptanceTest: Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```\nBoth `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` (delete \u2192 GET returns `deleted: true`) and `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` (recreate after delete succeeds) pass, and the full suite is green.\n\nNote: I left the count-based create checks (city capacity, daily limit, namesake count, household size) counting all rows, since the spec scoped the deleted-exclusion specifically to the duplicate/identity checks.",
